---
import InnerLayout from '../layouts/InnerLayout.astro';
import InnerBlock from '../components/inner/InnerBlock.astro';
import { SITE_URL, type PageSeo } from '../lib/seo';

const seo: PageSeo = {
  title: 'How We Work | Paradius LLC',
  description:
    'Two ways to buy, a reply within 24 hours, profiles within 48, and what happens when something goes wrong. Staff augmentation without the agency theater.',
  canonical: `${SITE_URL}/how-we-work/`,
  webPageName: 'How we work',
  webPageDescription:
    'The Paradius operating model for buyers: engagement models, timeline, continuity, replacement, IP and jurisdiction.',
};
---

<InnerLayout seo={seo} mode="two-sided">
  <InnerBlock force="power" kind="hero" title="How we work">
    <p>
      Every engineer we send was interviewed by the person who signs your contract. This
      page explains what that means in practice: what you are buying, how fast it starts,
      and what happens when something goes wrong.
    </p>
  </InnerBlock>

  <InnerBlock force="power" title="Two ways to buy">
    <p>
      <strong>Browse the registry.</strong> You pick engineers from our registry, interview
      them, and run them inside your team. You manage the day to day; we stay responsible
      for quality, continuity and replacement.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Start your team.</strong> You describe the outcome. We assemble the team, run
      the day to day, and answer for delivery. You set goals and review progress.
    </p>
    <p>There is no third model. We do not sell fixed bid projects.</p>
  </InnerBlock>

  <InnerBlock force="power" title="The process, with times">
    <ol role="list">
      <li>
        You write. Tell us who or what you need: the contact form, or
        <a href="mailto:solutions@paradius.dev">solutions@paradius.dev</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        We reply within 24 hours. A real reply from the principal, with matched profiles
        or precise questions. Never an autoresponder.
      </li>
      <li>
        Profiles within 48 hours. Anonymized, and verifiable in one call: stack, years,
        experience, languages. Full identity is disclosed later in the deal, off platform.
      </li>
      <li>
        The engagement starts. Every engineer begins under our hub discipline in Managua,
        Nicaragua, on Central Time with full overlap with US business hours: a senior
        mentor at the next desk, standards enforced from day one. Then they go remote, and
        nothing degrades, because the discipline travels with them.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </InnerBlock>

  <InnerBlock force="will" title="How we select">
    <p>
      No algorithmic screening. No credential theater. We examine the systems an engineer
      has built, not their resume. Then we talk: what they refuse to ship tells us more
      than what they list. The last filter is always the person who signs your contract.
    </p>
  </InnerBlock>

  <InnerBlock force="will" title="Continuity and replacement">
    <p>
      Every engineer passes a three month proving period with us before they ever reach a
      client, so a bad fit is rare. When it happens, say so: we transition to another
      engineer quickly, because context is documented and shared from day one. Context
      never lives in one head.
    </p>
    <p>
      And the question you are too polite to ask: what if Paradius disappears tomorrow?
      Nothing happens to you. Every system we build ships with documentation, repositories
      and credentials in your accounts. Your team keeps shipping. That is written into how
      we work, and it is why our clients' systems are still standing years after we left
      them.
    </p>
  </InnerBlock>

  <InnerBlock force="power" title="The paper">
    <p>
      Contracts are with Paradius LLC, registered in Wyoming, under US jurisdiction,
      billed in USD. The IP is yours from day one. NDAs are signed by default. Your
      systems carry no signature of ours.
    </p>
  </InnerBlock>

  <InnerBlock force="power" title="Pricing">
    <p>
      There is no pricing on this site because requirements determine price. A senior
      engineer embedded in a regulated bank is not a line on a rate card. Tell us what you
      need and we scope rates against your actual architecture, in private, within 24
      hours.
    </p>
  </InnerBlock>

  <InnerBlock force="power" kind="cta" title="Tell us who you need.">
    <p>We reply within 24 hours with matched profiles and a rate proposal.</p>
    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <a href="/talent" class="inner-button">Browse the registry</a>
      <a href="/contact" class="inner-button inner-button--secondary">Start your team</a>
    </Fragment>
  </InnerBlock>
</InnerLayout>
